# THE LOBBY. The place between rounds (M16).
#
# A CHECKER STRIP AT BOTH ENDS, and that is the whole reason this segment is
# shaped the way it is. The party is always in a corridor between two boundaries;
# the lobby's own two strips are its entry and its exit, so a section is bounded
# by the exit strip of one lobby and the entry strip of the next. Every rule the
# round machine has -- both walls, "is everyone across", who lived -- is expressed
# against those two rows and nothing else.
#
# TEN ROWS, WHICH IS 20 m. Long enough that four players can spread out and not be
# standing on each other while they pick a hat, short enough that walking its
# length between rounds is a breath rather than a commute. The first and last rows
# are the strips, so eight rows are actually livable.
#
# NO PARAPET SUPPRESSION AND NO HOLES. The lobby is the one place on this bridge
# where falling off is not a design element: the whole point is that it is
# somewhere to stand around. A player who walks off the edge here is a player
# taken away from the thing the lobby is for, and the drone return would put them
# back seconds later anyway -- so the walls are left on and the deck is solid all
# the way across. It is the only segment in the pool that can say that.
#
# THE RACK. One of each special at z3, spread the full width so it reads as a
# CHOICE rather than a conveyor you walk down collecting all four: a machine gun
# at x2, a grenade at x5, a mine at x9 and a shield at x12, with a rocket at x7 on
# the centre line. You leave with ONE, because the slot holds one -- see
# special_pool.
#
# HATS at z6, past the rack, four of them across the width. Hats are the score
# (see the round scorer), so which one you take is not a decision -- how many you
# can carry out is, and that is a question about the section, not about here.
#
# The rack deliberately breaks the rule playtest_bridge.seg states in its own
# header about not opening with a free armoury. A lobby IS the armoury; the cost
# is not scarcity, it is that everything you are carrying is gone the moment you
# fail to reach the next strip.

name = lobby
base_height = 0
width = 15
length = 10
tags = foot, lobby, safe

